From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:02:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: name why a scan is busy

Roaming's first test had a scan refused with -EBUSY while connected, and no
log says whether the driver refused it or the stack above never called it.
Print the driver's state when it refuses. No such line then means the
refusal came from above.

Part of the Wi-Fi daily-use plan, phase 4.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
index 0c3af5bef..b77eb8ca4 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
@@ -988,6 +988,12 @@ static int mt6797_mac_hw_scan(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, struct ieee80211_vif *vif
 	online = mac->join_data_phase && !mac->join_data_ended &&
 		 mac->join_channel_released && mac->join_sta_active && !mac->join_cleanup_requested;
 	if ((mac->scan_used && !online) || mac->scan_online || mac->scan_online_cancel) {
+		dev_info_ratelimited(wiphy_dev(hw->wiphy),
+				     "one-shot WLAN scan busy: used=%u data=%u ended=%u released=%u sta=%u cleanup=%u online=%u cancel=%u\n",
+				     mac->scan_used, mac->join_data_phase, mac->join_data_ended,
+				     mac->join_channel_released, mac->join_sta_active,
+				     mac->join_cleanup_requested, mac->scan_online,
+				     mac->scan_online_cancel);
 		ret = -EBUSY;
 		goto out;
 	}
@@ -1042,6 +1048,8 @@ static int mt6797_mac_hw_scan(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, struct ieee80211_vif *vif
 		    !mt6797_hif_recycle_sequences(mac->hif, mac->sequence_base))
 			mac->sequence = mac->sequence_base;
 		if (mac->sequence > 230) {
+			dev_info_ratelimited(wiphy_dev(hw->wiphy),
+					     "one-shot WLAN scan busy: sequence=%u\n", mac->sequence);
 			ret = -EBUSY;
 			goto out;
 		}
